    "recommendations": "• Trim shrubs that are growing directly against or touching the exterior walls of the structure.\n• Thin the vegetation surrounding the structure to create open gaps between plant groupings.\n• Remove any dead or dry ground vegetation that has accumulated close to the structure.\n• Keep shrubs near the structure low and separated from each other rather than growing together in continuous patches.\n• Clear overhanging branches or shrubs that crowd the single access route into the property.\n• Keep the driveway edges trimmed back so vehicles can pass through without obstruction.\n• Remove shrubs or ground vegetation that blocks sightlines along the driveway approach.\n• Clear a turning or staging area near the structure so vehicles are not forced to back out along the single access route.\n• Trim back vegetation along the rear of the structure to allow movement around all sides.\n• Remove ground vegetation that has grown up against fencing, outbuildings, or other structures on the property.\n• Keep irrigated plantings close to the structure low-growing and spaced apart rather than in dense groupings.\n• Move any stored materials, firewood, or debris away from the exterior walls of the structure."
